      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Solar Radiation - Daily Surface Energy\n\nDaily surface energy from solar radiation.\n\nSolar energy accumulated on south-faced horizontal to vertical tilted surfaces on the northern hemisphere at latitudes:\n- **0°N (Equator)**: Year-round applications possible due to sufficient winter radiation\n- **30°N**: Mixed seasonal applications\n- **60°N**: Primarily summer-time applications\n\n### Unit Conversions\n- 1 MJ = 0.278 kWh = 239 kcal = 948 Btu\n- 1 m² = 1550 in² = 10.764 ft²\n\n### Seasonal Considerations\nAt the equator there is enough radiation in winter time to consider year-round applications. In the northern hemisphere, applications typically require energy mainly during summer time."
